{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771169581284,"sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","part":{"id":"prt_c61ee984b001nbt8YbiX2Web92","sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","messageID":"msg_c61ee6aab001ICucCNszfbxhDR","type":"tool","callID":"call_ae7602a972b1458a8cb30c1a","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Check package.json config","prompt":"Read and analyze package.json and all configuration files to understand the project setup.\n\nLook for:\n1. package.json - dependencies, scripts, project metadata\n2. vite.config.ts - Vite configuration\n3. tsconfig.json - TypeScript configuration\n4. eslint.config.js - ESLint configuration\n5. .prettierrc.json - Prettier configuration\n\nProvide a summary of:\n- Build tools and frameworks used\n- Available npm scripts\n- Test configuration\n- Linting and formatting setup\n- Any important configuration details"},"output":"task_id: ses_39e11679cffe4QtrJSKxWrnlMx (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Project Setup Analysis\n\n### Overview\nThis is **Conway's Game of Life** - a strategic cellular automaton puzzle game built with React and TypeScript.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Build Tools and Frameworks\n\n### Core Dependencies\n- **React**: ^19.2.4 - Latest React 19 version\n- **React DOM**: ^19.2.4 - DOM rendering for React\n- **TypeScript**: ^5.9.3 - Modern TypeScript configuration\n\n### Build & Development Tools\n- **Vite**: ^7.3.1 - Fast build tool and dev server\n- **@vitejs/plugin-react**: ^5.1.4 - React plugin for Vite\n\n### Testing Framework\n- **Vitest**: ^4.0.18 - Fast unit testing framework\n- **@vitest/ui**: ^4.0.18 - UI for Vitest tests\n- **jsdom**: ^28.1.0 - DOM environment for testing\n- **@testing-library/react**: ^16.3.2 - React component testing\n- **@testing-library/jest-dom**: ^6.9.1 - Custom Jest matchers\n- **@testing-library/user-event**: ^14.6.1 - User interaction simulation\n\n---\n\n## 2. Available NPM Scripts\n\n### Development\n```bash\nnpm run dev              # Start Vite dev server\nnpm run build            # TypeScript compile + Vite build\nnpm run preview          # Preview production build\n```\n\n### Code Quality\n```bash\nnpm run lint             # Run ESLint\nnpm run typecheck        # TypeScript type checking (no emit)\nnpm run format           # Format with Prettier\n```\n\n### Testing\n```bash\nnpm run test             # Run tests in watch mode\nnpm run test:run         # Run tests once\nnpm run test:ui          # Run tests with UI interface\nnpm run test:coverage    # Run tests with coverage report\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Test Configuration\n\n**Test Environment**: jsdom (simulated browser environment)\n\n**Setup File**: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/test/setup.ts`\n- Imports `@testing-library/jest-dom` for custom matchers\n- Provides localStorage mock implementation for testing\n\n**Test Globals**: Enabled (no need to import `describe`, `it`, `expect`)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Linting and Formatting Setup\n\n### ESLint Configuration\nUsing the new ESLint flat config format with these plugins:\n- `@typescript-eslint/eslint-plugin` - TypeScript linting\n- `eslint-plugin-react-hooks` - React Hooks rules\n- `eslint-plugin-react-refresh` - Fast Refresh optimization\n- `eslint-plugin-react` - React specific rules\n- `eslint-plugin-prettier` - Prettier integration\n\n**Key ESLint Rules**:\n- TypeScript recommended rules enabled\n- React Hooks recommended rules enabled\n- `react-refresh/only-export-components`: Warn if components aren't optimized for Fast Refresh\n- `react/react-in-jsx-scope`: Disabled (not needed in React 17+ with JSX transform)\n- `react/jsx-uses-react`: Disabled\n\n**Target Files**: `**/*.{ts,tsx}`\n**Ignore Directories**: `dist`, `node_modules`, `coverage`\n\n### Prettier Configuration\n```json\n{\n  \"semi\": false,              // No semicolons\n  \"singleQuote\": true,        // Single quotes\n  \"tabWidth\": 2,              // 2 spaces indentation\n  \"trailingComma\": \"es5\",     // Trailing commas where valid in ES5\n  \"printWidth\": 100,          // Max line width 100\n  \"arrowParens\": \"always\"     // Always use parentheses around arrow function args\n}\n```\n\n**Format Command**: `prettier --write \"src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css,json,md}\"`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Important Configuration Details\n\n### Path Aliases\nBoth TypeScript and Vite are configured with these path aliases:\n```\n@/          → /src\n@components/ → /src/components\n@lib/       → /src/lib\n@types/     → /src/types\n@hooks/     → /src/hooks\n@styles/    → /src/styles\n```\n\n### TypeScript Configuration\n- **Target**: ES2020\n- **Module System**: ESNext\n- **Strict Mode**: Enabled\n- **Additional Strict Checks**:\n  - `noUnusedLocals`: Enabled\n  - `noUnusedParameters`: Enabled\n  - `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`: Enabled\n  - `noUncheckedSideEffectImports`: Enabled (TypeScript 5+)\n- **JSX**: `react-jsx` (new JSX transform, no need to import React)\n- **Module Resolution**: `bundler` (modern resolution strategy)\n\n### Project Metadata\n- **Name**: game_of_life\n- **Version**: 0.0.1\n- **License**: ISC\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/ochanomizu21/game_of_life_game.git\n- **Keywords**: game-of-life, cellular-automaton, react, typescript\n\n### Type Checking\n- ESLint globals include window, document, localStorage, sessionStorage, and test globals (describe, it, expect, vi)\n- DOM globals (HTMLCanvasElement, Touch, MouseEvent, TouchEvent) are declared\n- React is also declared as a global\n\n---\n\n## Summary\nThis is a modern React 19 + TypeScript project using Vite as the build tool and Vitest for testing. The configuration follows current best practices with strict TypeScript settings, proper path aliases, and comprehensive linting/formatting setup. The test environment is configured with jsdom and includes localStorage mocking for comprehensive component testing capabilities.\n</task_result>","title":"Check package.json config","metadata