{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771169602564,"sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","part":{"id":"prt_c61ee98030015gHePf4nyEgu49","sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","messageID":"msg_c61ee6aab001ICucCNszfbxhDR","type":"tool","callID":"call_734d08df55ea4a509e56f93f","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Study all spec files","prompt":"Exhaustively read and analyze ALL specification files in specs/ directory to understand the complete requirements for the Game of Life application. \n\nFor each spec file, provide:\n1. Summary of the main functionality required\n2. Key technical requirements\n3. Dependencies on other systems\n4. Implementation priority (if mentioned)\n\nThe spec files are:\n- audio-sonification.md\n- auto-advance-transitions.md\n- canvas-rendering.md\n- expert-settings.md\n- flux-management.md\n- grid-interaction.md\n- level-progression.md\n- movement-detection.md\n- phase-management.md\n- scoring-system.md\n- simulation-engine.md\n- ui-overlay.md\n- user-interaction.md\n\nProvide a comprehensive summary of all specifications in your final message."},"output":"task_id: ses_39e1167f2ffeElokvnRb0g32ox (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Comprehensive Analysis of Game of Life Specifications\n\nI've read and analyzed all 14 specification files. Here's a detailed breakdown of each:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Audio Sonification System (audio-sonification.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Generates real-time audio feedback using Web Audio API based on simulation events (births) and user interactions (draw/erase)\n- Maps sounds to spatial data (row positions determine pitch) and intensity (number of births determines volume)\n- Supports multiple waveform types for different sonic textures\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- `SoundEngine` interface with methods for enabled state, volume control, waveform selection, and sound playback\n- Pitch mapping formula: `pitch = (1 - avgRow / totalRows) * frequencyRange` (higher rows = higher pitch)\n- Lazy initialization of AudioContext (browser autoplay policy compliance)\n- Volume range: 0.0 to 0.5 (default 0.1), displayed as percentage\n- Polyphonic sound generation for concurrent events\n- Sound parameters: 50-200ms duration, exponential decay envelope\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Core simulation engine: Provides birth statistics (bornCount, average row position)\n- User interaction system: Triggers draw/erase sounds on cell placement/removal\n- UI/overlay system: Provides settings UI for volume, waveform, and enabled toggle\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Not explicitly mentioned, but appears to be a feature enhancement rather than core functionality\n\n---\n\n### 2. Auto-Advance Transitions (auto-advance-transitions.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Cinematic fade transition system between levels with 2.0s fade-out, 2.0s interstitial, and 2.0s fade-in\n- Skip functionality (Space/ESC) at any point during transition\n- Handles both success (level complete) and failure (game over) scenarios\n- Pauses transitions when browser tab becomes inactive (gameplay continues, but transitions pause)\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- State machine with 5 transition states: PLAYING, FADING_OUT, INTERSTITIAL, FADING_IN, READY\n- TransitionConfig interface with timing parameters and skip enabled flag\n- CSS-based opacity animations with ease-in-out easing\n- Full-screen black overlay with z-index above game, below modals\n- Level info display during interstitial with fade in/out text\n- 60fps CSS transitions with `will-change: opacity` optimization\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Phase management system: Coordinates with FINISHED phase and level transitions\n- Level progression system: Loads next level configuration during interstitial\n- Scoring system: Displays final scores during transition\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Not explicitly mentioned, but essential for polished game flow\n\n---\n\n### 3. Canvas Rendering System (canvas-rendering.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- High-performance HTML5 Canvas rendering of the Game of Life grid\n- Age-based neon color gradient system with glow effects\n- Dark neon theme with responsive cell sizing\n- Optional grid lines display with keyboard toggle\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- Cell age color mapping: Age 0 (cyan, 15px glow), Age 1-2 (React blue, 8px glow), Age 3-5 (magenta, 4px glow), Age 6+ (deep purple, 2px glow)\n- Background: `#0a0a0f`, Grid lines: `#1a1a2e`\n- Responsive cell sizing: 18px mobile (< 768px), 20px desktop (>= 768px)\n- CanvasConfig interface with DPR scaling using `window.devicePixelRatio`\n- Intensity metric for CSS ambient effects: `Math.min(activeCount / 500, 1)`\n- Optimized rendering pipeline with minimal context state changes\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Core simulation engine: Provides grid state and dimensions\n- UI/overlay system: Grid line toggle setting\n- User interaction system: Triggers redraws on cell changes\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Core - Essential for visual presentation\n\n---\n\n### 4. Expert Settings / Dev Panel (expert-settings.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Hidden configuration interface accessible via backtick key (`), menu path, or triple-tap gesture (mobile)\n- Allows tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging\n- Real-time updates without restart required\n- Import/export settings as JSON\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- MovementDetectionParams: centroidHistoryLength (default: 5), movementThreshold (default: 0.5), minClusterSize (default: 1)\n- ScoringParams: moverPointsPerGeneration (default: 10), oscillatorPointsPerGeneration (default: 2), scoreMultiplier (default: 1.0)\n- LevelGenerationParams: baseTimeSeconds (default: 45), timeIncrementPerLevel (default: 15), baseFlux (default: 20), difficultyScalingMode (TIME_ONLY | RESOURCE_ONLY | MIXED | EXTREME)\n- GridSizingParams: mobileCellSize (default: 18), desktopCellSize (default: 20)\n- localStorage persistence under key `gol-expert-settings`\n- Schema validation with Zod or similar\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Movement detection: Provides parameters for tracking configuration\n- Scoring system: Receives scoring parameters\n- Level progression: Receives level generation parameters\n- Canvas rendering: Receives grid sizing parameters\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Secondary - Useful for development and tuning, but not required for core gameplay\n\n---\n\n### 5. Flux Management (flux-management.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Resource management system with limited \"Flux\" for placing cells\n- Strategic choice between using Flux during planning phase vs. saving for running phase\n- Full refunds during PLANNING phase, no refunds during RUNNING phase\n- Visual and audio feedback for placement, removal, and insufficient resources\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- Initial allocation: 20 Flux per level (configurable via expert settings)\n- Placement cost: 1 Flux per cell in both phases\n- FluxState interface: current, initial, placed, removed\n- Validation rules: Can't place if Flux < 1, refunds only in PLANNING phase, add-only in RUNNING phase\n- HUD display with color coding (green/yellow plenty, orange <30%, red at 0)\n- Atomic operations to prevent race conditions with simulation step\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- User interaction system: Coordinates cell placement with Flux deduction\n- Phase management system: Enforces different rules per phase\n- Level progression system: Resets Flux each level\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Core - Fundamental game mechanic\n\n---\n\n### 6. Grid Interaction (grid-interaction.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Direct manipulation interface for placing/removing cells during PLANNING phase\n- Click-based interaction with cursor feedback\n- Minimum cells rule (START button disabled until >= 1 cell placed)\n- Mobile touch support with 44x44px minimum touch targets\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- GridInteraction interface: cellX, cellY, isPlaceable\n- Disabled during RUNNING and FINISHED phases\n- Coordinate calculation: `cellX = Math.floor((x - gridOffsetX) / cellSize)`\n- Cursor states: default, crosshair (placeable), forbidden (unplaceable), minus icon (removable)\n- Visual animations: fade-in (0.1s) for placement, shrink (0.15s) for removal\n- Event delegation for efficient click handling\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Flux management system: Validates Flux availability before placement\n- Phase management system: Disables interaction outside PLANNING phase\n- Canvas rendering system: Provides grid for interaction\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Core - Essential for user input\n\n---\n\n### 7. Level Progression (level-progression.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Progressive difficulty system with increasing time limits and constant Flux\n- Multiple difficulty scaling strategies configurable via expert settings\n- Automatic level advancement with fade transitions\n- No lose condition (always advances), only score varies\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- LevelConfig interface: levelNumber, timeLimitSeconds, initialFlux\n- Default time scaling: `45 + (levelNum - 1) * 15` seconds\n- Difficulty modes: TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME\n- LevelProgression state: currentLevel, maxUnlockedLevel, totalScore, levels array\n- Default 10 levels (configurable), victory screen after final level\n- Score accumulation across all levels (totalScore)\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Auto-advance transitions: Handles fade transitions between levels\n- Scoring system: Accumulates score across levels\n- Phase management system: Resets to PLANNING phase for each level\n- Expert settings: Provides difficulty scaling parameters\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Core - Fundamental to game structure\n\n---\n\n### 8. Movement Detection / Centroid Tracking (movement-detection.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Algorithmic system to detect and classify cellular movement patterns\n- Tracks connected cell clusters using 8-connectivity\n- Calculates centroids and classifies as MOVER, OSCILLATOR, or STATIC\n- Used by scoring system to award points per generation\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- CellCluster interface: id, cells (Set of \"x,y\" strings), centroid, generation\n- TrackedCluster extends CellCluster with centroidHistory, velocity, classification\n- Connected component detection with flood-fill or union-find algorithm\n- Centroid velocity calculation: `dx = (current.x - history[0].x) / historyLength`\n- Classification rules: MOVER (velocity > threshold), OSCILLATOR (static centroid, changing cells), STATIC (unchanging)\n- History tracking with configurable length (default: 5 generations)\n- Performance: Must process in < 16ms for 60fps with actual game grid sizes (20×30, 40×50, 60×80)\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Core simulation engine: Provides grid state for analysis\n- Scoring system: Provides cluster classifications for point calculation\n- Expert settings: Receives tracking configuration parameters\n\n**Implementation Priority:** High - Essential for scoring mechanics\n\n---\n\n### 9. Phase Management (phase-management.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- State machine governing three core game phases: PLANNING → RUNNING → FINISHED\n- Manages transitions with countdown between PLANNING and RUNNING\n- Coordinates with level progression for auto-advance\n- Guards phase transitions to prevent skipping\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- GamePhase type: 'PLANNING' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED' (plus implicit 'COUNTDOWN')\n- PhaseState interface: current, canTransition, blockers\n- PLANNING: Unlimited duration, cell placement allowed, START button enabled when >=1 cell\n- COUNTDOWN: 3-2-1 display, no input, simulation not running\n- RUNNING: Fixed timer, add-only cell placement, automatic simulation\n- FINISHED: Brief 2.0s pause, auto-advance to next level, view-only\n- Transitions: PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED → PLANNING (next level)\n- Timer uses Date.now() or performance.now() for accuracy\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Flux management: Different rules per phase (refunds in PLANNING, add-only in RUNNING)\n- Grid interaction: Disabled outside PLANNING phase\n- Level progression: Triggers on FINISHED phase\n- Scoring system: Active only during RUNNING phase\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Core - Central game state management\n\n---\n\n### 10. Scoring System (scoring-system.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Real-time score calculation based on pattern classifications from movement detection\n- Points awarded per generation: MOVER (10 pts), OSCILLATOR (2 pts), STATIC (0 pts)\n- Smooth score display with counting animation\n- Per-level score reset, high score persistence in localStorage\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- ScoringConfig: moverPointsPerGeneration (default: 10), oscillatorPointsPerGeneration (default: 2), scoreMultiplier (default: 1.0)\n- ScoreState: currentScore, generationScore, totalPatternsTracked\n- Calculation formula: Sum of pattern points × scoreMultiplier\n- Score cap: MAX_SAFE_INTEGER (9,007,199,254,740,991)\n- Real-time updates every generation with 0.2s lerp animation\n- Optional pattern breakdown display showing active movers/oscillators\n- End-of-level stats: final score, time survived, patterns created\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Movement detection: Provides TrackedCluster classifications\n- Phase management system: Active only during RUNNING phase\n- Level progression: Score accumulates across levels\n- Expert settings: Receives scoring parameters\n\n**Implementation Priority:** High - Core reward mechanism\n\n---\n\n### 11. Core Simulation Engine (simulation-engine.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Computes cellular automaton generations using Conway's Game of Life rules\n- Tracks cell ages for rendering purposes\n- Toroidal (wrap-around) boundary conditions\n- Optimized performance with React refs and precomputed neighbor offsets\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- GridType: number[][] (0 = dead, >0 = age in generations)\n- RuleSet: born=[3], survive=[2,3] (Conway standard)\n- Moore neighborhood (8 adjacent cells) with toroidal wrapping using modulo arithmetic\n- Double buffering for synchronous state updates\n- Simulation step process: copy grid → iterate cells → count neighbors → apply rules → swap buffers\n- Performance: Direct grid access via ref (not state), precomputed OPERATIONS array, generation counter for render triggering\n- Speed control: 10ms to 500ms between steps using requestAnimationFrame with delta time check\n- Audio integration: Track birth events (count and average row position)\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Canvas rendering: Receives grid state for visualization\n- Audio sonification: Receives birth statistics\n- User interaction: Modifies grid directly via ref\n- Movement detection: Analyzes grid for pattern classification\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Core - Fundamental simulation logic\n\n---\n\n### 12. UI/Overlay System (ui-overlay.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Cinematic intro overlay with glitch effect title and \"ENTER VOID\" CTA\n- Glass-morphism HUD with main controls, interaction modes, and status display\n- Settings panel with configuration options for all game systems\n- UI toggle for hiding/showing all interface elements\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- IntroState: isIntro, isExiting with 1.2s fade/scale exit animation\n- Glass HUD: semi-transparent (rgba 255,255,255,0.1) with backdrop-filter blur(10px)\n- Main control buttons: PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM (15% density), CLEAR (red text)\n- Interaction modes: DRAW, ERASE with active state highlighting\n- Status controls: Waveform selector (Sine/Triangle/Square/Saw), Volume slider (0-0.5), Generation counter, Settings toggle\n- Phase display: Shows PLANNING/COUNTDOWN/RUNNING/FINISHED, timer, Flux counter\n- Settings panel: Speed (10-500ms), Grid size buttons (20×30, 40×50, 60×80), Grid lines checkbox, Audio enable checkbox, Expert settings access\n- UIState: isUiVisible, isIntro, isExiting, showSettings, enableUI\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- All systems: Configurable via settings panel\n- Core simulation: Speed and size settings affect simulation\n- Audio system: Enable toggle controls sonification\n- Canvas rendering: Grid line option\n- User interaction: Mode buttons select draw/erase\n- Phase management: Phase display shows current state\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Core - Essential user interface\n\n---\n\n### 13. User Interaction System (user-interaction.md)\n\n**Summary of Main Functionality:**\n- Handles mouse and touch input for drawing and erasing cells on the grid\n- Supports drag-to-draw functionality with continuous placement\n- Prevents browser default behaviors (scroll/zoom) during interaction\n- Real-time sound feedback for each interaction\n\n**Key Technical Requirements:**\n- InteractionMode type: 'draw' | 'erase'\n- Coordinate mapping: `row = floor(y / (canvasHeight / numRows))`, `col = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`\n- Mouse events: mousedown, mousemove (while pressed), mouseup (global)\n- Touch events: touchstart, touchmove, touchend/cancel with preventDefault()\n- Interaction handler: type='down' for initial click, type='enter' for drag continuation\n- Cursor: crosshair style over canvas\n- Mobile: touch-action: none, ignore multi-touch beyond first\n- Sound integration: Different tones for draw vs. erase\n\n**Dependencies on Other Systems:**\n- Core simulation: Grid ref and dimensions for coordinate mapping\n- Audio sonification: Play interaction sounds\n- Canvas rendering: Redraw on state change\n- Flux management: Validate Flux availability\n- Phase management: Check if interaction allowed\n\n**Implementation Priority:** Core - Essential user input handling\n\n---\n\n## Overall Architecture Summary\n\nThe Game of Life application is a sophisticated cellular automaton simulation with gamification elements. Here's the dependency hierarchy:\n\n**Foundation Layer:**\n1. Core Simulation Engine - Grid computation with Conway's rules\n2. Phase Management - State machine controlling game flow\n3. Canvas Rendering - High-performance visualization\n\n**Mechanics Layer:**\n4. Flux Management - Resource system for cell placement\n5. Movement Detection - Pattern classification (MOVER/OSCILLATOR/STATIC)\n6. Scoring System - Points based on pattern activity\n\n**Interaction Layer:**\n7. User Interaction - Mouse/touch input handling\n8. Grid Interaction - Direct manipulation interface\n9. Audio Sonification - Sound feedback system\n\n**Meta Layer:**\n10. Level Progression - Multi-level structure with difficulty scaling\n11. Auto-Advance Transitions - Cinematic transitions between levels\n12. UI/Overlay System - Controls and configuration interface\n13. Expert Settings - Hidden dev panel for parameter tuning\n\n**Key Design Patterns:**\n- State machines for phase and transition management\n- Lazy initialization for browser policy compliance\n- React refs for performance-critical operations\n- localStorage persistence for settings and high scores\n- Responsive design with mobile/desktop variants\n\n**Priority Assessment:**\n- **Core (must-have):** Simulation Engine, Phase Management, Canvas Rendering, User Interaction, Flux Management, Grid Interaction, UI/Overlay\n- **High (should-have):** Movement Detection, Scoring System, Level Progression, Audio Sonification\n- **Secondary (nice-to-have):** Auto-Advance Transitions, Expert Settings\n</task_result>","title":"Study all spec files","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39e1167f2ffeElokvnRb0g32ox","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771169552393,"end":1771169602561}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771169607732,"sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","part":{"id":"prt_c61ee9830001ZwJ110h7BRg2ey","sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","messageID":"msg_c61ee6aab001ICucCNszfbxhDR","type":"tool","callID":"call_3c31121e9aa64497a92d1b9f","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Find test coverage","prompt":"Find and analyze all test files in the codebase to understand what has been tested.\n\nLook for:\n1. All *.test.ts and *.test.tsx files\n2. Test configuration files (vitest.config.ts, jest.config.js, etc.)\n3. Test setup files\n4. Test coverage reports if they exist\n\nFor each test file, provide:\n- File name and path\n- What functionality it tests\n- Number of tests\n- Any test failures or skipped tests\n\nCheck if there are any test scripts in package.json and if tests are currently passing."},"output":"task_id: ses_39e1167bbffeGArdaW40a7WFGt (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nPerfect! Now I have a complete picture of the test suite. Let me provide you with a comprehensive analysis.\n\n## Test Analysis Summary\n\n### Test Framework & Configuration\n\n**Test Runner:** Vitest v4.0.18  \n**Environment:** jsdom  \n**Test Setup File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/test/setup.ts`\n\nThe test setup file:\n- Imports `@testing-library/jest-dom` for DOM matchers\n- Mocks `localStorage` with a custom implementation to avoid browser-specific issues\n\n### Test Scripts in package.json\n\n```json\n\"test\": \"vitest\"           // Run tests in watch mode\n\"test:ui\": \"vitest --ui\"   // Run tests with UI\n\"test:run\": \"vitest run\"   // Run tests once\n\"test:coverage\": \"vitest run --coverage\"  // Run with coverage report\n```\n\n### All Test Files (10 total)\n\n| # | File Path | Tests | Status |\n|---|-----------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/App.test.tsx` | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n| 2 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.test.tsx` | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 3 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.test.tsx` | 14 | ✅ Pass |\n| 4 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/flux.test.ts` | 22 | ✅ Pass |\n| 5 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.test.ts` | 7 | ✅ Pass |\n| 6 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.test.ts` | 19 | ✅ Pass |\n| 7 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/phase.test.ts` | 20 | ✅ Pass |\n| 8 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/logger.test.ts` | 11 | ✅ Pass |\n| 9 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/validation.test.ts` | 27 | ✅ Pass |\n| 10 | `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/simulation.test.ts` | 30 | ✅ Pass |\n\n**Total Tests:** 157  \n**Test Results:** All 157 tests passing ✅\n\n---\n\n### Detailed Test File Analysis\n\n#### 1. **src/App.test.tsx** (3 tests)\n**Tests Main App Component rendering:**\n- Renders the title \"Conway's Game of Life\"\n- Renders all game controls (Small, Medium, Large, Start, Clear, Random, Draw, Erase)\n- Renders status display (Phase, Cells, Flux)\n\n#### 2. **src/components/GridInteraction.test.tsx** (4 tests)\n**Tests GridInteraction component:**\n- Renders without crashing with default props\n- Disables interaction during RUNNING phase (cursor: not-allowed)\n- Disables interaction during COUNTDOWN phase (cursor: not-allowed)\n- Enables interaction during PLANNING phase (cursor: default)\n\n#### 3. **src/components/CanvasGrid.test.tsx** (14 tests)\n**Tests canvas utility functions:**\n- **getCellColor**: Returns correct colors based on cell age (0=cyan, 1-2=blue, 3-5=magenta, 6+=purple)\n- **getCellBlur**: Returns correct blur values based on cell age (decreases as age increases)\n- **getResponsiveCellSize**: Returns 20px for desktop (>767px), 18px for mobile (≤767px)\n\n#### 4. **src/lib/flux.test.ts** (22 tests)\n**Tests Flux (budget/resource) system:**\n- **createInitialFluxState**: Creates flux state with default (20) or custom values\n- **canPlaceCell**: Checks if flux >= 1\n- **canRefundCell**: Only allows refunds during PLANNING phase\n- **placeCell**: Decrements flux, tracks placed cells, doesn't modify initial flux\n- **removeCell**: Increments flux and tracks removals (only in PLANNING phase)\n- **resetFlux**: Resets to initial value\n- **getFluxColor**: Returns green (plentiful), yellow (moderate), orange (<30%), red (0)\n\n#### 5. **src/lib/interaction.test.ts** (7 tests)\n**Tests grid interaction utilities:**\n- **getCellFromEvent**: Converts mouse/touch events to grid coordinates with canvas offset and DPR support\n- **isWithinBounds**: Validates coordinates are within grid dimensions\n- **createInitialInteractionState**: Creates initial state with mouse up\n\n#### 6. **src/lib/state.test.ts** (19 tests)\n**Tests Redux-like state management utilities:**\n- **createActionCreator**: Creates actions without payload\n- **createActionCreatorWithPayload**: Creates actions with payload\n- **createReducer**: Creates reducers with action handlers, handles unknown actions\n- **createAsyncAction**: Creates async action creators (request, success, failure)\n- **combineReducers**: Combines multiple reducers, only updates when state changes\n- **dispatchMultiple**: Dispatches multiple actions\n- **localStorage helpers**: saveToLocalStorage, loadFromLocalStorage, removeFromLocalStorage with error handling\n\n#### 7. **src/lib/phase.test.ts** (20 tests)\n**Tests game phase management:**\n- **canTransition**: Validates phase transitions (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED → PLANNING)\n- **getBlockers**: Returns blockers for phase transitions (needs cells, countdown active)\n- **createInitialPhaseState**: Creates initial PLANNING phase state\n- **phaseReducer**: Handles phase actions (START_COUNTDOWN, DECREMENT_COUNTDOWN, START_RUNNING, DECREMENT_TIMER, FINISH_PHASE, RESET_PHASE)\n\n#### 8. **src/lib/logger.test.ts** (11 tests)\n**Tests logger utility:**\n- **Logger.getInstance**: Returns singleton instance\n- **debug**: Logs debug messages with timestamp and context\n- **info**: Logs info messages\n- **warn**: Logs warning messages\n- **error**: Logs error messages with optional error object and stack trace\n- **formatMessage**: Formats messages with timestamp, level, and context\n\n#### 9. **src/lib/validation.test.ts** (27 tests)\n**Tests validation utilities:**\n- **isValidCoordinate**: Validates coordinates are within bounds\n- **clamp**: Clamps values within range\n- **isInRange**: Checks if value is within range\n- **isPositiveNumber**: Validates positive numbers (>0)\n- **isNonNegativeNumber**: Validates non-negative numbers (≥0)\n- **isInteger**: Validates integers\n- **isValidRuleSet**: Validates Conway's Game of Life rule sets (born/survive arrays)\n- **validateGridDimensions**: Validates grid dimensions (positive, max 1000x1000)\n\n#### 10. **src/lib/simulation.test.ts** (30 tests)\n**Tests Game of Life simulation core:**\n- **createGrid**: Creates grid with correct dimensions and initializes all cells to 0\n- **countNeighbors**: Counts neighbors with toroidal boundaries (wrap around)\n- **applyRules**: Applies Conway's rules (block pattern, glider pattern, age tracking, birth calculations)\n- **stepSimulation**: Increments generation counter, applies rules\n- **setCell**: Sets cell to specified age without mutation\n- **clearGrid**: Creates new empty grid\n- **randomFill**: Fills grid with random cells (default 15% density)\n- **countAliveCells**: Counts cells with age > 0\n- **isGridEmpty**: Checks if grid has any alive cells\n- **GRID_SIZE_PRESETS**: SMALL (20x30), MEDIUM (40x50), LARGE (60x80)\n- **getGridSize**: Returns grid size for preset\n\n---\n\n### Test Coverage Areas\n\n**Well-Tested Components:**\n1. **Core Simulation Logic** - Game of Life rules, neighbor counting, grid operations\n2. **State Management** - Redux-like utilities, localStorage persistence\n3. **Phase Management** - Game flow (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED)\n4. **Flux System** - Resource/budget management for cell placement\n5. **Validation** - Input validation, coordinate checking, rule set validation\n6. **UI Components** - Main App, GridInteraction, Canvas utilities\n7. **Interaction** - Mouse/touch event handling, coordinate conversion\n8. **Logging** - Debug, info, warn, error logging with context\n\n**Test Quality:**\n- ✅ All tests use descriptive names following best practices\n- ✅ Good separation of concerns (unit tests for utilities, integration tests for components)\n- ✅ Tests cover edge cases (boundary conditions, error states, invalid inputs)\n- ✅ Tests verify immutability where appropriate\n- ✅ Tests use mocking appropriately (vi.fn, localStorage mock)\n\n### Test Execution Results\n\n```\nTest Files: 10 passed (10)\nTests: 157 passed (157)\nDuration: 9.79s (transform 2.31s, setup 3.37s, import 3.63s, tests 2.28s, environment 38.74s)\n```\n\n**Status:** ✅ All tests passing  \n**Warnings:** \n- Some stderr output about HTMLCanvasElement.getContext() not being implemented (expected in jsdom environment)\n- Error messages in stderr are expected - they're from error handling tests that verify proper error logging\n\n### Recommendations\n\n1. **Coverage:** No coverage reports exist. Run `npm run test:coverage` to generate coverage reports and ensure adequate code coverage.\n\n2. **Additional Tests:** Consider adding integration tests for:\n   - End-to-end game flow (planning → countdown → running → finished)\n   - Complex patterns (gliders, spaceships, oscillators)\n   - Performance tests for large grids\n\n3. **Visual Regression Tests:** Consider adding visual regression tests for the canvas rendering.\n\n4. **Canvas Mocking:** The warnings about HTMLCanvasElement.getContext() could be resolved by adding canvas mock if needed for more detailed canvas tests.\n</task_result>","title":"Find test coverage","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39e1167bbffeGArdaW40a7WF