{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771169648120,"sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","part":{"id":"prt_c61f00dae001sZtg7O3jYODwCP","sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","messageID":"msg_c61efe110001fkOpUMbFFL6cbr","type":"tool","callID":"call_11934f1b3cdf4872b018ded4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: import { useState, useCallback } from 'react'\n2: import { createGrid, GRID_SIZE_PRESETS, type GridSizePreset } from '../lib/simulation'\n3: import { type GridType, type FluxState, type GamePhase, type InteractionMode } from '../types'\n4: import { createInitialFluxState } from '../lib/flux'\n5: import { GridInteraction } from './GridInteraction'\n6: \n7: export function Game() {\n8:   const [gridPreset, setGridPreset] = useState<GridSizePreset>('SMALL')\n9:   const [grid, setGrid] = useState<GridType>(() => createGrid(20, 30))\n10:   const [flux, setFlux] = useState<FluxState>(() => createInitialFluxState(20))\n11:   const [phase, setPhase] = useState<GamePhase>('PLANNING')\n12:   const [showGridLines, setShowGridLines] = useState(true)\n13:   const [interactionMode, setInteractionMode] = useState<InteractionMode>('DRAW')\n14: \n15:   const handleStart = useCallback(() => {\n16:     if (phase === 'PLANNING') {\n17:       setPhase('COUNTDOWN')\n18:     }\n19:   }, [phase])\n20: \n21:   const handleGridChange = useCallback((newGrid: GridType) => {\n22:     setGrid(newGrid)\n23:   }, [])\n24: \n25:   const handleFluxChange = useCallback((newFlux: FluxState) => {\n26:     setFlux(newFlux)\n27:   }, [])\n28: \n29:   const handleClear = useCallback(() => {\n30:     const { rows, cols } = GRID_SIZE_PRESETS[gridPreset]\n31:     setGrid(createGrid(rows, cols))\n32:     setFlux(createInitialFluxState(20))\n33:     setPhase('PLANNING')\n34:   }, [gridPreset])\n35: \n36:   const handleRandom = useCallback(() => {\n37:     const { rows, cols } = GRID_SIZE_PRESETS[gridPreset]\n38:     const newGrid = createGrid(rows, cols)\n39:     const density = 0.15\n40: \n41:     for (let row = 0; row < rows; row++) {\n42:       for (let col = 0; col < cols; col++) {\n43:         if (Math.random() < density) {\n44:           newGrid[row][col] = 1\n45:         }\n46:       }\n47:     }\n48: \n49:     setGrid(newGrid)\n50:     setFlux(createInitialFluxState(20))\n51:     setPhase('PLANNING')\n52:   }, [gridPreset])\n53: \n54:   const aliveCount = grid.flat().filter((cell: number) => cell > 0).length\n55: \n56:   return (\n57:     <div style={{ padding: '20px', backgroundColor: '#0a0a0f', minHeight: '100vh', color: '#fff' }}>\n58:       <h1 style={{ textAlign: 'center', marginBottom: '20px', color: '#61dafb' }}>\n59:         Conway's Game of Life\n60:       </h1>\n61: \n62:       <div style={{ marginBottom: '20px', textAlign: 'center' }}>\n63:         <div\n64:           style={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'center', gap: '10px', marginBottom: '10px' }}\n65:         >\n66:           <button onClick={() => setGridPreset('SMALL')} disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING'}>\n67:             Small\n68:           </button>\n69:           <button onClick={() => setGridPreset('MEDIUM')} disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING'}>\n70:             Medium\n71:           </button>\n72:           <button onClick={() => setGridPreset('LARGE')} disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING'}>\n73:             Large\n74:           </button>\n75:         </div>\n76: \n77:         <div\n78:           style={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'center', gap: '10px', marginBottom: '10px' }}\n79:         >\n80:           <button onClick={handleStart} disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING' || aliveCount === 0}>\n81:             {phase === 'PLANNING' ? 'Start' : 'Running'}\n82:           </button>\n83:           <button onClick={handleClear} disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING'}>\n84:             Clear\n85:           </button>\n86:           <button onClick={handleRandom} disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING'}>\n87:             Random\n88:           </button>\n89:         </div>\n90: \n91:         <div\n92:           style={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'center', gap: '10px', marginBottom: '10px' }}\n93:         >\n94:           <button onClick={() => setShowGridLines(!showGridLines)} disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING'}>\n95:             {showGridLines ? 'Hide Grid' : 'Show Grid'}\n96:           </button>\n97:         </div>\n98: \n99:         <div\n100:           style={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'center', gap: '10px', marginBottom: '10px' }}\n101:         >\n102:           <button\n103:             onClick={() => setInteractionMode('DRAW')}\n104:             disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING'}\n105:             style={{ backgroundColor: interactionMode === 'DRAW' ? '#61dafb' : '#1a1a1a' }}\n106:           >\n107:             Draw\n108:           </button>\n109:           <button\n110:             onClick={() => setInteractionMode('ERASE')}\n111:             disabled={phase !== 'PLANNING'}\n112:             style={{ backgroundColor: interactionMode === 'ERASE' ? '#61dafb' : '#1a1a1a' }}\n113:           >\n114:             Erase\n115:           </button>\n116:         </div>\n117:       </div>\n118: \n119:       <div style={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'center', marginBottom: '20px' }}>\n120:         <div\n121:           style={{\n122:             display: 'flex',\n123:             gap: '30px',\n124:             padding: '10px 20px',\n125:             backgroundColor: 'rgba(26, 26, 46, 0.8)',\n126:             borderRadius: '8px',\n127:             backdropFilter: 'blur(10px)',\n128:           }}\n129:         >\n130:           <div>Phase: {phase}</div>\n131:           <div>Cells: {aliveCount}</div>\n132:           <div\n133:             style={{\n134:               color: flux.current > 10 ? '#00ff00' : flux.current > 5 ? '#ffaa00' : '#ff0000',\n135:             }}\n136:           >\n137:             Flux: {flux.current}\n138:           </div>\n139:         </div>\n140:       </div>\n141: \n142:       <div style={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'center' }}>\n143:         <GridInteraction\n144:           grid={grid}\n145:           flux={flux}\n146:           phase={phase}\n147:           showGridLines={showGridLines}\n148:           onGridChange={handleGridChange}\n149:           onFluxChange={handleFluxChange}\n150:           interactionMode={interactionMode}\n151:         />\n152:       </div>\n153:     </div>\n154:   )\n155: }\n156: \n\n(End of file - total 156 lines)\n</content>","title":"src/components/Game.tsx","metadata":{"preview":"import { useState, useCallback } from 'react'\nimport { createGrid, GRID_SIZE_PRESETS, type GridSizePreset } from '../lib/simulation'\nimport { type GridType, type FluxState, type GamePhase, type InteractionMode } from '../types'\nimport { createInitialFluxState } from '../lib/flux'\nimport { GridInteraction } from './GridInteraction'\n\nexport function Game() {\n  const [gridPreset, setGridPreset] = useState<GridSizePreset>('SMALL')\n  const [grid, setGrid] = useState<GridType>(() => createGrid(20, 30))\n  const [flux, setFlux] = useState<FluxState>(() => createInitialFluxState(20))\n  const [phase, setPhase] = useState<GamePhase>('PLANNING')\n  const [showGridLines, setShowGridLines] = useState(true)\n  const [interactionMode, setInteractionMode] = useState<InteractionMode>('DRAW')\n\n  const handleStart = useCallback(() => {\n    if (phase === 'PLANNING') {\n      setPhase('COUNTDOWN')\n    }\n  }, [phase])\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771169648056,"end":1771169648116}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771169673902,"sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","part":{"id":"prt_c61f00da5001W4LbAQ8zBq0O7r","sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","messageID":"msg_c61efe110001fkOpUMbFFL6cbr","type":"tool","callID":"call_bfa34acd8a5847b096c72332","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Identify highest priority tasks","prompt":"Based on IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md and the current codebase state, identify the most important next items to implement.\n\nFocus on:\n1. Sprint 2 items marked as HIGH priority\n2. Items that block other features\n3. Items that would provide the most value to users\n\nFor each item, provide:\n- Item name and location in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n- Why it's important\n- Dependencies (what needs to exist first)\n- Estimated difficulty\n\nPrioritize by importance and dependencies.","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"task_id: ses_39e0ff253ffezItNoZRZCHhzTe (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md and current codebase (Sprint 1 complete), here are the most important next items:\n\n---\n\n## 1. Movement Detection (Sprint 2.4) - HIGHEST PRIORITY\n**Location:** IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:332-357 → src/lib/movement.ts\n\n**Why important:** \n- Blocking dependency for Scoring System and Level Progression\n- Core gameplay mechanic requiring algorithmic complexity (connected components, centroid tracking, classification)\n- Performance-critical (must be <16ms for 60fps)\n\n**Dependencies:** simulation-engine, type definitions ✅ (complete)\n\n**Estimated difficulty:** HIGH (complex algorithms, performance optimization)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scoring System (Sprint 2.5) - HIGH PRIORITY\n**Location:** IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:359-390 → src/lib/scoring.ts\n\n**Why important:**\n- Core game loop (motivation for players)\n- Required for Level Progression\n- Provides immediate feedback/engagement\n\n**Dependencies:** movement-detection (item #1 above), type definitions ✅\n\n**Estimated difficulty:** MEDIUM (straightforward calculations, UI display)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Intro Overlay (Sprint 2.1) - HIGH PRIORITY\n**Location:** IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:259-277 → src/components/IntroOverlay.tsx\n\n**Why important:**\n- First impression - sets tone\n- Creates cinematic experience\n- Blocks full game flow (must happen before game starts)\n\n**Dependencies:** Canvas rendering ✅, UI state management ✅\n\n**Estimated difficulty:** MEDIUM (CSS animations, state management)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Main UI Controls (Sprint 2.2) - HIGH PRIORITY\n**Location:** IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:279-310 → src/components/GlassHUD.tsx, UIToggleButton.tsx\n\n**Why important:**\n- Full player control interface\n- Settings access (gear icon)\n- Mode switching (draw/erase)\n- Speed control\n\n**Dependencies:** Phase management ✅, all systems ✅\n\n**Estimated difficulty:** MEDIUM (component composition, responsive design)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Phase Status Display (Sprint 2.3) - HIGH PRIORITY\n**Location:** IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:312-330 (integrated into GlassHUD)\n\n**Why important:**\n- Game visibility (players need to know phase/timer)\n- Critical for player decision-making\n- Part of unified HUD\n\n**Dependencies:** Phase management ✅, Flux management ✅\n\n**Estimated difficulty:** LOW (simple display, already exists in Game component)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Settings Panel (Sprint 2.6) - HIGH PRIORITY\n**Location:** IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:392-416 → src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx\n\n**Why important:**\n- Player customization\n- Speed/grid/audio controls\n- Expert settings access\n\n**Dependencies:** All systems ✅ (currently hardcoded, need UI exposure)\n\n**Estimated difficulty:** MEDIUM (modal/sidebar UI)\n\n---\n\n## Critical Path Order:\n\n1. **Movement Detection** → prerequisite for scoring\n2. **Scoring System** → prerequisite for levels\n3. **Intro Overlay** → first impression\n4. **Main UI Controls** (includes Phase Display) → full control\n5. **Settings Panel** → customization\n\n**Parallelizable after #2:** Intro Overlay + Main UI Controls can be built together since they don't block each other.\n</task_result>","title":"Identify highest priority tasks","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39e0ff253ffezItNoZRZCHhzTe","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771169648041,"end":1771169673900}}}}
