{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771169689335,"sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","part":{"id":"prt_c61f0aecb001rdZVQyvEdTfXXI","sessionID":"ses_39e11aa4effeYeEII0I39dpUo4","messageID":"msg_c61f0993f001mmiqB9BGMV2vMA","type":"tool","callID":"call_5e104e6a5da14d2a9955264d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/movement-detection.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/movement-detection.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Movement Detection (Centroid Tracking)\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Algorithmic system to detect and classify cellular movement patterns by tracking centroids of connected cell clusters over time.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Connected Component Detection\n9: Identify clusters of adjacent live cells using 8-connectivity (include diagonals):\n10: \n11: ```typescript\n12: interface CellCluster {\n13:   id: string;                    // Unique identifier (e.g., hash of coordinates)\n14:   cells: Set<string>;             // Set of \"x,y\" coordinate strings\n15:   centroid: { x: number; y: number };  // Average of all cell positions\n16:   generation: number;             // When this cluster was first identified\n17: }\n18: \n19: function findConnectedComponents(grid: boolean[][]): CellCluster[];\n20: ```\n21: \n22: ### Centroid Tracking\n23: Track cluster centroids across generations to calculate velocity:\n24: \n25: ```typescript\n26: interface TrackedCluster extends CellCluster {\n27:   centroidHistory: { x: number; y: number }[];  // Last N centroids\n28:   velocity: { dx: number; dy: number };         // Calculated movement vector\n29:   classification: 'MOVER' | 'OSCILLATOR' | 'STATIC';\n30: }\n31: \n32: interface TrackingConfig {\n33:   historyLength: number;        // Generations to track (expert setting, default: 5)\n34:   movementThreshold: number;      // Min distance to be considered moving (default: 0.5 cells)\n35: }\n36: ```\n37: \n38: ### Classification Algorithm\n39: For each cluster with sufficient history:\n40: \n41: 1. **Calculate Centroid Velocity**: \n42:    - `dx = (current.x - history[0].x) / historyLength`\n43:    - `dy = (current.y - history[0].y) / historyLength`\n44: \n45: 2. **Classify**:\n46:    - **MOVER**: `|dx| > threshold` OR `|dy| > threshold` (centroid is translating)\n47:    - **OSCILLATOR**: Centroid static (within threshold) BUT cell set changes between generations (cells are moving locally)\n48:    - **STATIC**: Centroid static AND cell set unchanged\n49: \n50: 3. **Cluster Persistence**:\n51:    - Match clusters across generations by nearest centroid\n52:    - Handle cluster splits/merges (edge case: when two gliders collide)\n53: \n54: ## UI/UX Requirements\n55: \n56: ### Performance Indicators\n57: - Show \"active patterns\" count in HUD\n58: - Highlight moving patterns with subtle glow effect\n59: \n60: ## Edge Cases\n61: \n62:  1. **Cluster Split**: One cluster becomes two (e.g., glider collision) - track both as new clusters or attempt lineage?\n63:  2. **Cluster Merge**: Two clusters become one - classification reset to avoid double-counting\n64:  3. **Oscillator Period Detection**: Blinker has period 2, Pulsar has period 3 - centroid stays same but cells swap\n65:  4. **Glider Guns**: Stationary structure producing moving gliders - gun is Static, produced gliders are Movers\n66:  5. **Minimum Cluster Size**: Single isolated cell - treat as cluster of size 1 or ignore?\n67:  6. **Large Grid Performance**: With 100x100 grid (performance benchmark, not a game configuration), expect ~50-200 clusters max - must process in < 16ms for 60fps\n68: \n69: ## Implementation Notes\n70: \n71: - Run connected component analysis every generation during RUNNING phase\n72: - Store cluster history in circular buffer (efficient memory usage)\n73: - Use Manhattan distance or Euclidean for centroid matching\n74: - Performance requirements must scale with actual game grid sizes (20×30, 40×50, 60×80)\n75: - Optimization: Only recompute centroids for changed regions, not full grid\n76: - Memory: Limit history buffer size to prevent unbounded growth\n77: \n\n(End of file - total 77 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/movement-detection.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Movement Detection (Centroid Tracking)\n\n## Overview\nAlgorithmic system to detect and classify cellular movement patterns by tracking centroids of connected cell clusters over time.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Connected Component Detection\nIdentify clusters of adjacent live cells using 8-connectivity (include diagonals):\n\n```typescript\ninterface CellCluster {\n  id: string;                    // Unique identifier (e.g., hash of coordinates)\n  cells: Set<string>;             // Set of \"x,y\" coordinate strings\n  centroid: { x: number; y: number };  // Average of all cell positions\n  generation: number;             // When this cluster was first identified\n}\n\nfunction findConnectedComponents(grid: boolean[][]): CellCluster[];\n```","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771169689294,"end":1771169689327}}}}
